	"description": [
		"For science majors, learning to read the primary literature found in scientific journals is an important transition from classroom learning to post-graduate endeavors. Students enrolled in this course will read, present and discuss current scientific papers in a field selected by participating faculty. The goal is to garner sufficient expertise in the particular field to allow critical analysis of the scientific literature. Requires permission of instructor. May be repeated if topics are different."
